{% doc %}
  The age question, everywhere except the product page.

  ── Why it is rendered from the layout ────────────────────────────────
  Same reason sv-card-wish is: the question belongs to the shopper, not
  to one template. A parent can arrive on a collection from Instagram, on
  search results from Google, or on the homepage from a card — and until
  now only the product page ever asked them what size they were shopping
  for. One render keeps the wording, the storage and the behaviour from
  drifting between them.

  The product page keeps its own copy: it does more with the answer
  (it pre-selects a variant), so sv-product.js owns that dialog and this
  snippet stands down there entirely.

  ── Where the bands come from ─────────────────────────────────────────
  Admin's navigation — the same third level the chip rows read, so the
  labels in the dialog and the labels on the shelf can never disagree,
  and each band carries the collection it lands on. Nothing is typed
  here.

  ── When it asks unprompted ───────────────────────────────────────────
  On a shelf: collections, search results, the collection index. Not on
  the homepage, which opens on the film and then asks the same question
  in full as its first section — a dialog over that is the question asked
  twice. Not on cart, account or policy pages, where the shopper is
  finishing something. The dialog is still RENDERED on those pages so a
  "change" control keeps working; it just does not open by itself.

  @param {string} [menu] - Menu whose third level holds the size links
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign menu_handle = menu | default: 'main-menu'
  assign nav = linklists[menu_handle]

  assign labels = ''
  assign band_json = '['
  assign n = 0

  for link in nav.links
    for band in link.links
      for chip in band.links
        assign parts = chip.url | split: '/'
        assign tag = parts.last
        assign head = tag | slice: 0, 4
        if head != 'age-'
          continue
        endif

        assign probe = chip.title | append: '|'
        if labels contains probe
          continue
        endif
        assign labels = labels | append: probe

        assign j_label = chip.title | json
        assign j_tag = tag | json
        assign j_url = chip.url | json
        if n > 0
          assign band_json = band_json | append: ','
        endif
        assign band_json = band_json | append: '{"label":' | append: j_label
        assign band_json = band_json | append: ',"tag":' | append: j_tag
        assign band_json = band_json | append: ',"url":' | append: j_url | append: '}'
        assign n = n | plus: 1
      endfor
    endfor
  endfor

  assign band_json = band_json | append: ']'
  assign labels = labels | split: '|'
-%}

{%- if n > 1 -%}
  {%- liquid
    # Which size this shelf is already narrowed to, if any. Read by
    # prefix, because a filtered URL can also carry a garment type.
    assign active_tag = ''
    for t in current_tags
      assign head = t | slice: 0, 4
      if head == 'age-'
        assign active_tag = t
        break
      endif
    endfor

    assign ask = false
    if template.name == 'collection' or template.name == 'search' or template.name == 'list-collections'
      assign ask = true
    endif

    assign page = 'other'
    if template.name == 'collection' and collection != blank
      assign page = 'collection'
    endif
  -%}

  {{ 'sv-age.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  {%- render 'sv-agepick', id: 'global', bands: labels, page: page -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    The band table is handed over as data rather than written into the
    script file, because it is Admin's menu and changes without a deploy.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script>
    (() => {
      const d = document.querySelector('dialog[data-sv-age]');
      if (!d) return;
      d.dataset.bands = {{ band_json | json }};
      d.dataset.activeTag = {{ active_tag | json }};
      d.dataset.ask = {{ ask | json }};
      {%- comment -%}
        A type shelf — Rompers & Onesies, Co-ord Sets — can be narrowed by
        size too: its own tag URL keeps the type AND filters the size,
        which is what a parent asked for. The shelf's own tag list comes
        with it so the script can tell "we make that here" from "we do
        not" before sending anyone anywhere; without it an empty size
        would land them back on the whole shelf, showing every size to
        someone who just named one.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      d.dataset.shelfUrl = {% if collection %}{{ collection.url | json }}{% else %}""{% endif %};
      {%- comment -%}
        `| default:` stringifies an array, which shipped a comma-joined
        list where JSON was expected — branch instead.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        dataset values are strings: assigning the array itself gave a
        comma-joined list, which JSON.parse then choked on. Stringify it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      d.dataset.shelfTags = JSON.stringify({% if collection %}{{ collection.all_tags | json }}{% else %}[]{% endif %});
    })();
  </script>
  <script src="{{ 'sv-age.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}
